{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/932968-crunch-for-unspecified-merits-new-st-here","id":932968,"title":"Crunch for unspecified Merits (new ST here)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-17T10:54:48-07:00","id":932968,"title":"Crunch for unspecified Merits (new ST here)","content":"Hi all, I'm new to the whole Chronicles of Darkness system, and will be the Storyteller for our upcoming campaign. Still working on teaching myself the system.<br /> <br /> Am having some confusion on a number of things that don't have any specified crunch in the book. As an example - the Thief of Fate merit. <br /> <br /> Using this in a test combat last night, there was a lot of confusion. The Merit description just says that the user &quot;steals fortune&quot; from their target, but I can't find any actual details anywhere on how to implement this. <br /> <br /> Is there someplace that provides detail on this that I'm not finding, or am I supposed to just make something up as to how this works in game?<br /> <br /> Any guidance would be appreciated. Thanks for your help!<br /> <br /> Valerie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12106-digigirl","name":"Digigirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:07:56-07:00","id":932975,"title":"","content":"The mechanics for Thief of Fate are given in the sentence that immediately follows: whenever you touch a person without spending Willpower to suppress the effect, then for the rest of the day, they suffer dramatic failures instead of normal failures, and you gain +4 dice instead of +3 when you spend Willpower to boost your dice pool. That's what it does, that's how you steal fortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:16:25-07:00","id":932977,"title":"","content":"Thanks. For some reason, the way you just described it makes it much more clear to me than the way it is worded in the book. Appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12106-digigirl","name":"Digigirl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}